# Force LF line endings for scripts that run on Kabré/Linux. SLURM's sbatch
# refuses batch scripts with CRLF ("Batch script contains DOS line breaks"),
# and a shebang line with a trailing \r breaks execve() ("bad interpreter").
# Without this, editing these files on Windows (even via tools that respect
# core.autocrlf) can silently reintroduce CRLF and break every future run.
*.sh text eol=lf
*.slurm text eol=lf
Makefile text eol=lf
*.mk text eol=lf
